    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d362">

                <pb facs="0470" n="388" sameAs="frus:frus1865p3/pg388"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Bigelow</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 86.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Departmrnt of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-03-27"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 27, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatch of the 10th of March, No. 52,
                    which is accompanied by a translation of a circular issued by the minister of
                    foreign affairs of the Archduke Maximilian, relative to consuls in Mexico, who
                    have no exequaturs from the imperial government, has been received. I have
                    already sufficiently explained our position on this subject.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Bigelow,</hi> Esq., <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
